Subject: [PATCH 10569/11362] Widen three QA-layer guards that were narrower
 than their own concepts (REQ-VERIFY-6802)

From the 2026-08-31 QA-layer audit (19 SILENT_NON_FIRING, 7 NEEDS_REDESIGN). Six
findings covered these files; each was TRIAGED by running the reviewer's own
missed input against the live guard rather than believing the report.

FOUR CONFIRMED, TWO REFUTED. `_legitimate_pair` returns False for the cited pair,
so the tautology check does fire. `_inference_substrate_text` returns
'prod-eastus-17' from the principle-wrapped dict, so it does read through the
wrapper -- notable because that function was a July origin bug, so the reviewer
may be pattern-matching history rather than current code. 4/6 is why findings are
tested, not trusted.

Three fixed:

  `roc_auc` does not contain "auroc" as a substring, so the commonest sklearn
  spelling of the headline metric was invisible: {"roc_auc": 1.0, "n_samples":
  400} drew no flag at all.

  check_sign_anomaly's increase-expected list omitted rates, so a pass rate
  falling 0.80 -> 0.60 drew nothing.

  int({"principle":..., "value": 0}) RAISES TypeError, so a principle-wrapped
  level_credit_delta REMOVED the guard instead of failing it closed -- the July
  origin class, fixed in a sibling function and not this one.

I GOT THE BLAST-RADIUS MEASUREMENT WRONG FIRST AND CORRECTED IT. An initial scan
claimed 44 artifacts newly flagged. Spot-checking showed both examples flagged on
`violations` and `delta` -- pre-existing fields, unrelated to the addition. I had
compared "flags now" against "not stamped", and unstamped does not mean the check
was silent. The correct A/B, the same corpus through the module with and without
the two added names, reports ZERO newly flagged across 1,500.

The fourth confirmed finding is NOT fixed here: `_has_compute_bound_marker` misses
experiment_746_dualgpu_eorm_jepa_retrain (verdict "dualgpu_retrain_validated",
duration_s=1.73, no marker matched). Fixing it means matching verdict prose, a
wider blast radius that deserves its own measurement.

spec-coverage refused the first attempt: the new tests had no REQ. Added
REQ-VERIFY-6802 with three scenarios and cited it, rather than leaving the tests
untraceable.

7 tests, each the audit's own missed input. 3/3 mutations RED. 114 adjacent
adversarial tests pass.

